{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream","id":821719,"title":"Nightmares & Dreamscapes: Incursions from the Primordial Dream","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-02T10:33:24-08:00","id":821719,"title":"Nightmares & Dreamscapes: Incursions from the Primordial Dream","content":"The title is pretty much self-explainatory: this is a thread I made to post all sorts of critters and oddities born from the Primordial Dream. Think <b>Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss. </b>There's not exactly a schedule behind this, I have many ideas in mind but nothing too definite. I'll simply post stuff when I feel like I have something decent to share. <div align=\"center\"><br /> <b>Entry #1: The Night Terrors</b></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> (Guess who has read Innocents again)<br /> <br /> The Primordial Dream is a dark ocean given shape by the collective fears of mankind. Within it, the Chambers and Burrows of infinite Lairs give home to countless Horrors, echoes of traumatized minds that merged with fundamental narratives and the souls of Beasts. Beast themselves are atavistic nightmares incarnate, something that reaches deep into the psyche of man and shakes it from its foundation. In the Primordial Dream Beasts are apex predators, something so powerful that their mere presence alters the oniric landscape around them and bleeds into the dreams of others.<br /> <br /> There are smaller things out there.<br /> <br /> One kind of minor inhabitants of the Primordial Being are the so-called Night Terrors. Night Terrors embody smaller fears. It's not like those fears count less, it's just that the Night Terrors are smaller. They're limited, superficial. The Night Terrors don't reflect those fears in the same deep, primordial way a Horror does. A Horror's nature covers broad concepts and the nightmares it manifests reach the roots of the human experience,. A Night Terror's nature does not. They're are simpler creatures, a cluster of immediate reactions and phobias that has gained a semblance of sentience. There's no lesson to be learned from the Night Terrors, they just are. Night Terrors don't have a Lair, their soul is what they bring with themselves, not something they can externalize. Most of them die soon after their birth, reabsorbed by the Primordial Dream or devoured by Horrors and other entities. Their limited power, though, allows them to move furtively across the Dream and even slip into Lairs. Night Terrors see Horrors as the major predators of their nightmarish ecosystem and istinctively surrend themselves to them. Since Night Terrors cannot feed as easily as Horrors do, they aim to create a relationship with them not much different from that between a pilot fish and a shark. Night Terrors help Horrors feed and keep the Lairs clean while at the same time they gain protection, a home, access to the Primordial Pathways that lead the material world and, obviously, the chance to feed on the snippets left by the Horror or go hunting in the surrounding area.<br /> <br /> The mind of Night Terrors is an extremely basic conglomerate of primary reactions. Their personality is not a proper answer to a humand mind but rather a web of fragmented fears, distorted emotions and elementary impulses.Many Night Horrors find easier to feed on children, as they are more vulnerable to their tricks, but also because they find them easier to understand, their way to react to the world more immediate and clear than that of adults. According to most scholars of the Primordial Dream, Night Terrors are a natural occurrence, little parasites born out the ripples in the darkness. Others think that the seeds of what will grow into a Night Terror are sowed whenever a Beast breaks a mind while using its powers. Whatever the case, Beasts as a whole don't see them as a problem. There's not a huge amount of them and don't breed as parasites do. They happen and that's about it. If a Beasts adopts them, Night Terrors can be helpful and loyal. If that's not the case, they're easily dispatched. Without a Beast that offers them protection, Night Terrors are practically powerless.<br /> <br /> <b>Traits</b><br /> <br /> <b>Legend: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors have Legend, but not Life, and regain Willpower as normal. They don't need to sleep and they do not refresh Willpower through rest. Acting according to their Legend is the only way they can regain Willpower</span></span></span><br /> <b>Attributes: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors use the ephemeral beings attributes</span></span><br /> <b>Speed: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">as usual, with many adding some sort of \u201cspecies factor\u201d to it</span></span><br /> <b>Size: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Varies; some are small as rats, some are larger than adults</span></span><br /> <b>Corpus: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Varies by Size</span></span><br /> <b>Rank: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Most Night Terrors are Rank 1, sometimes 2, with a few extremely rare ones reaching Rank 3</span></span><br /> <b>Common Manifestation: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nightmare Apparition</span></span><br /> <b>Common Numina: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Emotional Aura, Hallucination, Sign</span></span><br /> <b>Nightmares: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Most Night Terrors can replicate the effects of a Nightmare or two</span></span><br /> <b>Ban: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Different Night Terrors have different Bans, based on the fears they incarnate. A Terror Under The Bed might not hurt those hidden under the sheets, The Thing In The Closet has no Defense if there's a light in the room (even a nightlight), The Creepy Clown flees from those who laugh...</span></span><br /> <b>Bane: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Bane of Night Terrors is related to their nature, like their Ban</span></span><br /> <b>Symbiotic Relationship: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors are strange and disconcerting. Most Beasts do not enjoy their presence and simply throw them away from their Lair or eliminate them in the same way one would do with pests. For those who tolerate them, though, Night Terrors can prove useful. When a Night Terror enters a Lair, the Beast istinctively notices it. The Horror reacts immediately to this intrusion and moves inside the Chambers to meet the unexpected visitor. It's at this point that the Beast can decide whether she agrees to accept this symbiotic relationship or not. If that's the case, the Night Terror gains immunity to the Lair Traits, adapting to its new home. When inside it, Night Terrors protect the Lair from hostile intruders and fight fiercely to defend the Horror and the Heart. Curiously, Night Terrors don't attack other Night Terrors: they recognize them as Family, and hope that the Horror will accept them as well. Truth be told, a Lair which holds a Night Terror seem to attract others of its kind. Additionally, when a Ravenous Horror goes on rampage, the Night Terrors help it. Whenever a Horror inflicts nightmares, roll the Night Terror's Power + Finesse. The Horror gains a number of bonus dices equal to the successes obtained. This bonus is cumulative among multiple Night Terrors, which mean the chances of Exceptional Success can get dangerously high. If a Lair collapses or merges with the Beast, Night Terrors will attempt to flee before it's too late.</span></span><br /> <b>Satiety: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors are simple beings, their personality a conglomeration of basic desires, an almost childlike approach to the world and traces of little fears and nightmares, but they retain enough free will to have a Satiety score. There's not much they want to do outside feeding, but they are naturally curious and some Beasts train them as some sort of twisted pet, perhaps hoping they could be eventually used as scouts or spies. The Night Terrors Satiety's score is slightly different from that of a Beast, ranging from 0 to 5 (1-2 Low, 3 Medium, 4 High, 5 Maximum). Night Terrors use Satiety to activate powers and heal when inside a Lair. They also loose a Satiety point each week.</span></span><br /> <b>Regaining Satiety: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors regain the same amount of Satiety the Horror gains when inflicting nightmares (that's why they help the Horror, an exceptional success means feeding a lot). When bonded with a Beast, they can also go hunting on their own. They roll Power + Rank \u2013 Composure to do so, sometimes adding a dice or two when the Beast they're bonded with is really strong (Lair 8+). On an Exceptional Success, they drag the victim to their Beast's Lair and the Horror hunts them as if it took them there in the first place. High and Maximum Satiety Horrors simply ignore those preys, with no additional result: no extra Satiety, no Soul Shocked Condition. Heroes can still attempt to track it, though.</span></span><br /> <b>Under the Bed: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors are way less mobile than Beasts, but can use Under the Bed in the same way a Beast does, rolling Power + Satiety instead of Presence + Satiety. They have no way to get the bonus from blood relatives, obviously.</span></span><br /> <b>Invade Dreams: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors can invade dreams just as Unfettered Beasts do.</span></span><br /> <b>Heroic Tracking: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Night Terrors can help the Horror feed, but they also disturb the Primordial Dream to a degree, meaning that Heroes can perceive their actions. Heroes who sense Night Terrors are not attracted to them, not exactly, but rather to the Horror they gravitate around. Night Terrors are too metaphysically small to be noticed on a long distance, but they can lead a Hero after their masters. The ripple created by Night Terrors is weaker (some sort of tracking malus is appropriate when going after them instead of a proper Beast), the only exception being when the Night Terrors obtain an Exceptional Success when inflicting nightmares. On those occasion, the Horror comes into play and the nightmares are so strong that Heroes can sense them as usual.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Sample Night Terrors</b></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Twisted Rabbit</b><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><i>&quot;C</i></span></span><i>ome out, come out, wherever you are!&quot;</i><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Twisted Rabbit is a nasty little thing that loves to haunt the rooms of children. He is a creature born from the cold, dead eyes of toys and the sinister appearance they take once the lights go out and you try to sleep. Twisted Rabbit itself resembles a pink rabbit doll who never blinks, his clothes covered in blood and a rusty knife in a hand. His favourite tactic is to take possession of a toy and wander in the room while the child is inside the bed. He hides some toys, damages others and changes position when nobody is watching, always getting closer. Twisted Rabbit never physically hurts kids, and sees what it does as the thing he's supposed to do. He's a creepy puppet who wants to play, scaring the crap out of children is part of the game.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Legend: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Uncanny</span></span></span><br /> <b>Attributes: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Power 2, Finesse 4, Resistance 1</span></span><br /> <b>Willpower: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5</span></span><br /> <b>Speed: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">7</span></span><br /> <b>Size: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1</span></span><br /> <b>Corpus: </b>2<br /> <b>Rank: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">1</span></span><br /> <b>Manifestations: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nightmare Apparition, Fetter (Open Condition related to toys), Unfetter</span></span><br /> <b>Numina: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Emotional Aura, Innocuous, Sign</span></span><br /> <b>Nightmares: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">They Are All Around You (The Toys Are Watching)</span></span><br /> <b>Ban: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Twisted Rabbit cannot use any Numina or Power as long as the victim is holding another puppet.</span></span><br /> <b>Bane: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Hunting rifles</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>The Disembodied Brain</b><br /> <i>&quot;Look at them, mere ants waiting to be enslaved by our superior intellects. So simple and yet so fascinating&quot;</i></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As its name suggests, the Disembodied Brain is a brain, eyeballs attached, that flies around nonchalantly, a peculiar sight indeed. It was spawned by a combination of visceral fears, phobia of surgery and clinical anxiety. The Brain is a prideful creature that loves to scare others and impose its will upon them. This Night Terror acts with malice and enjoys hurting others or forcing them to cut themselves. For all his arrogance, it is also a coward, and retreats hastily if menaced. The Disembodied Brain mostly targets the weak or those who can't defend themselves, seeing them as an easy prey and a funny way to satisfy its ego.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Legend: </b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Arrogant</span></span></span><br /> <b>Attributes: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Power 5, Finesse 4, Resistance 3</span></span><br /> <b>Willpower: </b>7<br /> <b>Speed:</b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> 11 (flying)</span></span><br /> <b>Size: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2</span></span><br /> <b>Corpus: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">5</span></span><br /> <b>Rank: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">2</span></span><br /> <b>Manifestations: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Nightmare Apparition, Discorporate, Reaching, Image</span></span><br /> <b>Numina: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Blast, Dement, Hallucination, Telekinesis</span></span><br /> <b>Nightmares: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Bugs Everywhere! (Viscera Everywhere!), You Must Obey (Obey the Brain!)</span></span><br /> <b>Ban: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Brain is deathly afraid of surgeons and doctors. It will flee immediately if it recognizes one of them.</span></span><br /> <b>Bane: </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Any jar big enough to trap it</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-02-2016, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":18}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:42:43-08:00","id":821764,"title":"","content":"Would you be OK with other people posting creature ideas on this thread? Because if so, I have few ideas. One of which would be Protogenoi, the gods of the Dark Dream. These would be as far beyond Horrors as they are beyond Night terrors and embody primordial fears in their entirety, as opposed to Horrors, which represent a facet of those fears.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-02-2016, 02:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:50:50-08:00","id":821775,"title":"","content":"This is really excellent Cinder, and the exact sort of thing that I was thinking Beast needed. I like the concept of the Primordial Dream, especially with how it fits into the Astral, but wish there was more information about the things that are there. I love the symbiotic relationship of these lesser terrors. Kudos!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T11:58:30-08:00","id":821780,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=821764#post821764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would you mind at all if other people posted dream-creatures on this thread?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, not at all. Just promise me they won't be <i>that </i>much better than mine, my already lacking self-esteem and ever present need for acknowledgement would not endure it.<br /> <br /> Seriously though, go for it <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T12:00:21-08:00","id":821782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=821775#post821775\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is really excellent Cinder, and the exact sort of thing that I was thinking Beast needed. I like the concept of the Primordial Dream, especially with how it fits into the Astral, but wish there was more information about the things that are there. I love the symbiotic relationship of these lesser terrors. Kudos!</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I was so caught up in my own idea that I forgot to say what I thought of the Night Terrors. I agree with leetsepeak on this. I'll have a lot of fun coming up with weird little critters to infest the Dark Dream now. I've an idea for a relatively powerful Terror (that's Rank 3) who comes to the Brood and asks them to help it evolve into a Horror. I think you could have fun trying to symbolically change its fear from something relatively trivial to something that can resonate in the deepest, darkest parts of the soul of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-02T12:03:59-08:00","id":821785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=821780#post821780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, not at all. Just promise me they won't be <i>that </i>much better than mine, my already lacking self-esteem and ever present need for acknowledgement would not endure it.<br /> <br /> Seriously, though, go for it <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. And I'm not sure I could do any better. Yours are really good.<br /> <br /> In relation to the Protogenoi, they could easily start off a plot. I see them as very much 'sleeping gods'. Waking them would require a vast amount of their attendant fear. Like, on the level of the Protogenoi of drowning requiring millions to drown within a relatively small area (like, for example, a coastal city) in order to wake.<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 02-02-2016, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T01:45:57-08:00","id":822196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=821785#post821785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks. And I'm not sure I could do any better. Yours are really good.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nonsense. You write good stuff. I know. <i>I'm watching. </i><br /> <br /> Anyways, if we want to make this a community thread like the Idigam one in the Werewolf forum so we all have a place to post our creatures from the Primordial Dream I won't have anything to object<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=821785#post821785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In relation to the Protogenoi, they could easily start off a plot. I see them as very much 'sleeping gods'. Waking them would require a vast amount of their attendant fear. Like, on the level of the Protogenoi of drowning requiring millions to drown within a relatively small area (like, for example, a coastal city) in order to wake.<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll be honest, I think I get what you're aiming for. Correct me if I'm wrong, but they're like some sort of Maeljin of nightmare, top-of-chain creatures that resonate with fear on the broadest possible level. It's a rough comparison, but gives the idea. The thing is, where the Shadow has the Maeljin and the Abyss has the Annunaki, I feel like these guys come dangerously close to a thematic space that should belong to the Dark Mother. I'm probably seeing it in an uncorrect way and you'll have a clear niche for them in mind but, if that's not the case, I do think it's better to avoid stepping on the Dark Mother's toes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-03-2016, 06:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T02:52:50-08:00","id":822224,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822196#post822196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'll be honest, I think I get what you're aiming for. Correct me if I'm wrong, but they're like some sort of Maeljin of nightmare, top-of-chain creatures that resonate with fear on the broadest possible level. It's a rough comparison, but gives the idea. The thing is, where the Shadow has the Maeljin and the Abyss has the Annunaki, I feel like these guys come dangerously close to a thematic space that should belong to the Dark Mother. I'm probably seeing it in an uncorrect way and you'll have a clear niche for them in mind but, if that's not the case, I do think it's better to avoid stepping on the Dark Mother's toes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That closeness to the Dark Mother was intentional. They're meant to be the intermediaries between Her and the Begotten, creatures of godlike power, so much that they require enormous sacrifice to wake for a short while, let alone remain awake. If the creatures of the Primordial Dream were compared to the descent from the original Chaos of Greek mythology, the Horrors would be the Titans and the Protogenoi would be the Primordials, beings which not only ruled over but actually embodied aspects of reality. The line between the fear of drowning and the Protogenos of drowning is so fine that it's essentially semantics. The idea of them was that they could serve to impress upon the Begotten the sheer power of the Dark Mother. If her Firstborn were this mighty, how great was She? The Dark mother does not represent fear, She <i>is </i>fear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T03:09:48-08:00","id":822234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822224#post822224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That closeness to the Dark Mother was intentional. They're meant to be the intermediaries between Her and the Begotten, creatures of godlike power, so much that they require enormous sacrifice to wake for a short while, let alone remain awake. If the creatures of the Primordial Dream were compared to the descent from the original Chaos of Greek mythology, the Horrors would be the Titans and the Protogenoi would be the Primordials, beings which not only ruled over but actually embodied aspects of reality. The line between the fear of drowning and the Protogenos of drowning is so fine that it's essentially semantics. The idea of them was that they could serve to impress upon the Begotten the sheer power of the Dark Mother. If her Firstborn were this mighty, how great was She? The Dark mother does not represent fear, She <i>is </i>fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, now I understand. Well, that's a greater scheme of things I can be intrigued about. I still have some small reservations, but color me interested.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-03-2016, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T04:25:09-08:00","id":822254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822234#post822234\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, now I understand. Well, that's a greater scheme of things I can be intrigued about. I still have some small reservations, but color me interested.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>You said you had reservations. Do you think you could give me some constructive criticism about this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:09:59-08:00","id":822280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822254#post822254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You said you had reservations. Do you think you could give me some constructive criticism about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing major. It's more a matter of personal taste, my own headcanon about the Dark Mother and my perception of how she was presented in the corebook. Silly things that only make me think it would be difficult to pull the Progenoi off in way that does not clash with my own subjective intepretation of the setting. All in all, not the sort of stuff that should influence your idea, which is solid and has plenty of potential.<br /> <br /> I reserve myself the right to be pleasantly surprised, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T05:19:45-08:00","id":822286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822224#post822224\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That closeness to the Dark Mother was intentional. They're meant to be the intermediaries between Her and the Begotten, creatures of godlike power, so much that they require enormous sacrifice to wake for a short while, let alone remain awake. If the creatures of the Primordial Dream were compared to the descent from the original Chaos of Greek mythology, the Horrors would be the Titans and the Protogenoi would be the Primordials, beings which not only ruled over but actually embodied aspects of reality. The line between the fear of drowning and the Protogenos of drowning is so fine that it's essentially semantics. The idea of them was that they could serve to impress upon the Begotten the sheer power of the Dark Mother. If her Firstborn were this mighty, how great was She? The Dark mother does not represent fear, She <i>is </i>fear.</div> </div> </div> </div> So, you're talking about the idea that these guys ARE Anakim, Makara, Namtaru and the like? Interesting...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:03:52-08:00","id":822303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ZealousChristian24</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822286#post822286\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, you're talking about the idea that these guys ARE Anakim, Makara, Namtaru and the like? Interesting...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, sort of. There are greater and lesser Protogenoi. The greater are Anakim, Makara and Namtaru. The lesser are fears within those. For example, within Anakim there is The Mighty, the embodiment of unstoppable strength, there is Judgement, the manifestation of inescapable consequences and there is the Triad, the three women who represent inevitable Fate. There are more than just these of course, but you get the idea I hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T06:04:28-08:00","id":822305,"title":"","content":"The Protogenos of drowning would be a Lesser Protogenos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T22:54:26-08:00","id":823091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=822254#post822254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You said you had reservations. Do you think you could give me some constructive criticism about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't speak for <b>Cinder</b>, but I'm not really seeing a niche for &quot;protogenoi&quot;. For example, the idea that they act as intermediaries to the Dark Mother - considering how active she is, is that really necessary? Each chapter of the corebook has her dropping in one of the Begotten, offering encouragement . . . or making an example out of some poor arrogant schmuck. When your goddess can (and does) show up whenever she wants, a priesthood is a bit redundant. . . . unless they can help keep her <i>away</i>. <br /> <br /> Going with too regimented a hierarchy also seems to undermine the inchoate nature of the Primordial Dream. If there are clear power rankings . . . I don't know, its just that if you can catalog the denizens of the Dream, making sense of (and thus bringing order to) what's inherently irrational and surreal . . . It seems to violate the core premise of the place.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of a thread of various creatures, Chambers, and nightmares people have come up with, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T23:15:50-08:00","id":823100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>One Vorlon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=823091#post823091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I can't speak for <b>Cinder</b>, but I'm not really seeing a niche for &amp;quot;protogenoi&amp;quot;. For example, the idea that they act as intermediaries to the Dark Mother - considering how active she is, is that really necessary? Each chapter of the corebook has her dropping in one of the Begotten, offering encouragement . . . or making an example out of some poor arrogant schmuck. When your goddess can (and does) show up whenever she wants, a priesthood is a bit redundant. . . . unless they can help keep her <i>away</i>. <br /> <br /> Going with too regimented a hierarchy also seems to undermine the inchoate nature of the Primordial Dream. If there are clear power rankings . . . I don't know, its just that if you can catalog the denizens of the Dream, making sense of (and thus bringing order to) what's inherently irrational and surreal . . . It seems to violate the core premise of the place.<br /> <br /> I do like the idea of a thread of various creatures, Chambers, and nightmares people have come up with, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's your view, fair enough. I'm going to carry on with the Protogenoi but it's your choice if you want to use them. I'm not quite sure what you mean when you say that the Dark Mother turns up fairly often. From what I got in the book, the Begotten see Her at their Devouring and usually spend a lot of time looking for Her. And I meant that the Protogenoi were intermediaries between Horrors and the Mother in power, not that they were messengers or some kind of priesthood. It's just that they are more powerful than the Begotten and less so than the Dark Mother.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T00:57:08-08:00","id":823147,"title":"","content":"Just need to point this out: I kinda feel bad that it looks like I disapproved the Protogenoi. I would not dare to tell someone that one of their ideas is bad and that they're wrong for pursuing it. Especially not in the context of homebrew and fanmade stuff, where I wrote some pretty silly things in the past and will probably continue to do so in the future.<br /> <br /> Write what you think would be cool and don't let my vague feelings influence you in the slightest. The Protogenoi are probably going to be good, if not necessarily my cup of tea. But, you know, screw me, I'm not anyone's boss nor a competent critic.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: One Vorlon expressed some some of my doubts better than I could articulate. The rest is mostly just based on my headcanon. I guess we'll see how things will turn out. And I think he refers to the &quot;Tales of the Dark Mother&quot; fiction at the the beginning of each chapter. All little stories where She makes an appearance, in a way or the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-04-2016, 05:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:10:20-08:00","id":824980,"title":"","content":"OK, I'm making headway in the write-up for the Protogenoi. For mechanics (those that are weak enough to need them *cough*rank 5*cough*) I was going to work off of the Unbound Horrors. I was considering having them be able to use Atavisms, but being able to use the Satiety Expenditure versions by paying Essence. Does that sound OK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:27:52-08:00","id":824986,"title":"","content":"It does sound identical to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774753-homebrew-hack-for-unfettered-beasts#post774753\">this hack</a> of mine for the Unfettered.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I can see it working.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T10:45:26-08:00","id":825003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deionscribe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=824986#post824986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It does sound identical to <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/774753-homebrew-hack-for-unfettered-beasts#post774753\">this hack</a> of mine for the Unfettered.<br /> <br /> But yeah, I can see it working.<br /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div> Oh, sorry, I had forgotten. D'you mind if I use it? I'll probably change it a little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:08:46-08:00","id":825015,"title":"","content":"Go ahead <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T11:58:23-08:00","id":825037,"title":"","content":"Yup, that might be a solid starting point.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure what idea to develop next: you'd rather have more critters or some weird phenomena?<br /> <br /> I seriously have so many ideas about Beast that I don't know where to start. Good things that most of my projects for other gamelines are postponed until I get the new books","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T12:26:04-08:00","id":825056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=825037#post825037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yup, that might be a solid starting point.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm not sure what idea to develop next: you'd rather have more critters or some weird phenomena?<br /> <br /> I seriously have so many ideas about Beast that I don't know where to start. Good things that most of my projects for other gamelines are postponed until I get the new books</div> </div> </div> </div>I had another idea for inhabitants of the Dream, Hollow Men. Basically, they're what happens when a human loses their soul. It's born of their numbness and emptiness. I'm not sure exactly how they'd look though.<br /> <br /> Something that would be very nice to have would be an actual description of how the PD works. The ones in the PDFs aren't very definitive. Some phenomena would be nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-08T09:10:39-08:00","id":826023,"title":"","content":"I dig the Night Terrors, Cinder. They feel very appropriate and give the Dream a sense of ecosystem. Plus, they immediately inspired me to come up with one: little, nearly invisible jellyfish that play off the fear and confusion of being hurt by something you can't see.<br /> <br /> Anyway, other things that might exist in the Primordial Dream. How about creatures influenced by old, dark emotions other than fear? What happens when a Horror picks up (or is born with) a taste for hatred or despair?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-10T09:32:29-08:00","id":827571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=826023#post826023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I dig the Night Terrors, Cinder. They feel very appropriate and give the Dream a sense of ecosystem. Plus, they immediately inspired me to come up with one: little, nearly invisible jellyfish that play off the fear and confusion of being hurt by something you can't see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! Something I tried to to keep in mind while writing is to leave them as variable and customizable as Beasts. It's not like I created something insanely original, but the amount of little critters you can come up with when you use the Night Terrors is frankly ridicolous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=826023#post826023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, other things that might exist in the Primordial Dream. How about creatures influenced by old, dark emotions other than fear? What happens when a Horror picks up (or is born with) a taste for hatred or despair?</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. You intend this as the emotion that spawned the Horror, or as something that follows weird Hungers? For all we know right now, the Primordial Horror is all about fear, but I sure can see some space for oddities that rely on a combination of fear and other emotions. Makes for some cool story hooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-10-2016, 03:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T08:37:38-08:00","id":828806,"title":"","content":"<div align=\"center\"><b>Sorrows</b><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Well you do enough talk<br /> My little hawk, why do you cry?<br /> Tell me what did you learn from the Tillamook Burn<br /> Or the Fourth of July?<br /> We're all gonna die.&quot;</i><br /> --Sufjan Stevens, <i>Fourth of July</i></div> <br /> Fear is hardly the only emotion humans feel. Though terror dominates the Primordial Dream, manifestations of other sentiments can occasionally be found flitting through the ethereal space of unconsciousness. Though still quite rare compared to Horrors, the most common of these anomalies might be the creatures known as Sorrows.<br /> <br /> There are two competing theories about the origin of Sorrows: Either they are spawned wholecloth in the Primordial Dream from nightmares of loss, despair, and regret, or they are hapless Horrors who strayed a little too close to the Bright Dream, becoming infected with one of humanity's more &quot;refined&quot; sentiments. Sadness can be seen as noble, after all, in ways fear never would be.<br /> <br /> No matter their genesis, Sorrows act much in the same way as Horrors; they stalk the Primordial Dream for dreaming prey on which to fill their bellies. Inflicting sorrow is often less a single shock, however, and more a drawn-out game. The Sorrow hunkers down in one dreamer's mindscape, and waits, subtly and gradually sowing the seeds of regret and despair.<br /> <br /> <b>Appearance:</b> The forms of Sorrows are usually less overtly monstrous than those of Horrors, a little less primal in their awfulness. A number have humanoid shapes, albeit strange and forbidding miens still. Even more are hazy and indistinct, as if viewed through a thick veil of tears. Many are cold to the touch. When they do take the form of mythological monsters, Sorrows tend to focus on the secondary characteristics ascribed to these creatures beyond what can kill a man: religious iconography, an aura of incense, large, mournful eyes.<br /> <br /> <b>Traits:</b> Sorrows are built similarly to the Unfettered. They are ephemeral entities with no connection to the flesh of the world. There is no memory or record of a Sorrow ever devouring the soul of a human and creating a Beast; one might imagine the results would be messy and unfortunate. <br /> <br /> If the Dark Mother has any opinion on these half-children of grief, she has not made her feelings known.<br /> <br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Like Horrors, each Sorrow pursues a hunger for power, hoard, prey, punishment, or ruin. The end goal is to inflict sadness rather than fear, and so feeding methods diverge.<br /> <br /> <b>Collectors</b> always look for objects of great sentimental value. Nothing quite stings like losing an irreplaceable memento. They take love letters, wedding rings, urns filled with the ashes of dead relatives, and family pets. This isn't to say that they overlook monetary value in their ministrations: In some dreams, the month's rent check goes missing, or the Sorrow mugs the dreamer of last ten dollars to her name. When the victim wakes, she may find herself clutching her possessions ever closer, or she may decide that material attachments are meaningless in the face of the great void that awaits her.<br /> <br /> <b>Nemeses</b> feed off shame and guilt. They follow the dreamer around, constantly reminding him of what he did, and why he should feel bad about it. Some take on the shapes of someone the dreamer hurt. Others look like judges on high, ready to mete out harsh sentencing for crimes real or imagined. In the aftermath of a devastating feeding, a dreamer may turn himself over to the authorities out of self-loathing and the belief that he was going to get caught anyway, so why waste everyone's much more valuable time?<br /> <br /> <b>Predators</b> of Sorrow are master manipulators. Unlike Horrors, they can't feed from directly hurting their prey; that's not how one feels sadness. Instead, they have to get the prey to hurt themselves. They get into the prey's head, show him how worthless his life is, how he's already peaked and everything is a downward slide from here. There's only one rational thing he can do, and the Sorrow is more than happy to provide the means to the unfortunate dreamer. Feeding doesn't always involve tackling the only valid philosophical problem, though. Some convince dreamers to neglect their bodies, relationships, or pursuits by making them feel hollow and meaningless. The aftermath of a successful feeding of this kind can be brutal: the Soul Shocked are not the most emotionally stable of individuals. A rash of suicides in Seattle in the nineties was traced back to a high-Rank ravenous Sorrow that required the efforts of the entire Hive to dispatch (though not before it forced the city's Apex to hang herself in shame at one she had allowed to come to pass).<br /> <br /> <b>Ravagers</b> have a relatively easy time of things: They set up a dream where someone the dreamer cares about dies, and then wait. Some fast-forward to the funeral, and inflict their victim with the realization that their loved ones won't be around forever, and neither will the dreamer. Everyone she cares about will die, and then she will die. Why fight it? Why care at all? Ravagers who target the non-living take a similar, relentless approach. The dream begins with the victim's house blowing down in a violent storm. She rebuilds it, only for the storm to destroy it again, and again, over and over until the dreamer finally gives up and lies down in the cold. The malaise that follows in the wake of these dreams can last for days when executed right.<br /> <br /> <b>Tyrants </b>must, as one would expect, dominate the dreamer in some way, though they rule not through fear of what they'll do to their victim, but by making the victim feel like he has no other choice but to obey. They make him feel small, unintelligent, powerless. Listen to me, you can't do this on your own. It's only logical that you obey me. You're only resisting because of your own, petty ego. Why are you so selfish? After waking, victims of these Sorrows tend to be plagued with self-doubt, especially those in positions of authority.<br /> <br /> <b>SOME SAMPLE SORROWS</b><br /> <br /> <b>The Glacial King</b><br /> <i>&quot;Do not fight it. You cannot fight it. You are so small compared to the glacier, so weak compared to the winter winds. Lie down. Give up now.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> The Glacial King takes the form of a tall, solidly-built old man with frostbitten gray skin, a stomach-length white beard, and gnarled fingernails, wrapped in a deep blue silk robe and topped with a crown of iron and ice. He is enshrouded in a permanent mantle of freezing air and bitter wind. He exists to make dreamers feel weak and inadequate in the face of uncaring reality, convincing them to give up on everything and embrace the cold.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 3<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Prey<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Pitiless<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 6, Finesse 4, Resistance 7<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 13<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 10<br /> <b>Size:</b> 6<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 20<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Despair 2, Winter 1<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Nightmare Apparition, Materialize<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Invade Dream, Aggressive Meme, Stalwart<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Fulfill Hunger for Prey<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Chemical fires<br /> <br /> <b>Squirming Screamer</b><br /> <i>&quot;Liar! Thief! Whore! How DARE you!&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> Squirming Screamer appears as a black, writhing ovoid scribble, or perhaps a hairball, or maybe a colony of daddy long-legs. In the center of its body lies a swollen, red eye that constantly twitches back and forth as it looks every which way. It worms its way into people's dreams and does what it does best: scream at them in disgust and disappointment for their shortcomings.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 1<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Punishment<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Shrill<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 3, Finesse 3, Resistance 3<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 8<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 6<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 10<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Guilt 1<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Nightmare Apparition<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Dement, Invade Dream<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Fulfill Hunger for Punishment<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Children's laughter<br /> <br /> <b>The Jilter</b><br /> <i>&quot;I know it's been a while. Come to bed. Take off your clothes first, I want to see you naked again. Oh, hmm.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> <b>Description:</b> While floating through the Primordial Dream, the Jilter is a blank, white humanoid shape whose edges are ragged and undulant. When it steps into a victim's dream, however, it instinctively takes on the form of a former lover, or sometimes an unrequited crush, either way someone who caused the dreamer romantic anguish, and who maybe he eventually got over, but toward whom he still harbors some secret longing and misery. The Jilter takes full advantage of this, tugging at the dreamer's heartstrings, reminding him why things didn't work out between him and his beloved, or hinting that maybe now, things will be different. The Sorrow brings back the pain of rejection, and the realization that even after all this time, his old object of affection still holds his heart in the palm of their hands. Well, it's the Jilter's heart now, to do with as it pleases.<br /> <br /> <b>Rank:</b> 2<br /> <b>Hunger:</b> Power<br /> <b>Legend:</b> Seductive<br /> <b>Attributes:</b> Power 3, Finesse 7, Resistance 2<br /> <b>Corpus:</b> 7<br /> <b>Willpower:</b> 9<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Essence:</b> 15<br /> <b>Influences:</b> Heartbreak 1, Lust 1<br /> <b>Manifestations:</b> Twilight Form, Nightmare Apparition, Image<br /> <b>Numina:</b> Invade Dream, Drain, Emotional Aura, Innocuous<br /> <b>Ban:</b> Fulfill Hunger for Power<br /> <b>Bane:</b> Proof that the dreamer has moved on from the lover the Jilter represents<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:04:21-08:00","id":828871,"title":"","content":"Just wanted to say that I think that's a great job. A meager Like is not always enough to express appreciation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T11:31:46-08:00","id":828887,"title":"","content":"Thanks! Glad you think so. I might add in examples of a Collector and Ravager Sorrow later on today.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-12T12:17:38-08:00","id":828912,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Seems like today is a productive day for this thread. Here's a phenomena. For the next one, I'll probably get back on creatures.</span></span> <div align=\"center\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Entry #2: The Nightmare Maelstrom</b></span></span></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">The cold, hard truth about the Primordial Dream is that nobody can truly predict its influence. It answers to rules and laws that are so buried within the darkest corners of the collective human experience and so removed from the reality of today's life that hoping to understand it would be a treacherous endeavour at best. While its language is something made of pure and unbridled strength that still refuses to waver even in the modern world, the Primordial Dream speaks to the atavistic and primeval parts of our souls. Even Beasts, born as they are with an innate connection to the nightmarish dimension, have a hard time at grasping the patterns of the Primordial Dream as a whole. They sure are the most fitting for the task, but obtaining a truly complete understanding of the oniric structure of the Primordial Dream, supposing that such structure does indeed exist, might be a feat that belongs more to the Dark Mother than her children. This means that, whether they like it or not, the Primordial Dream sometimes holds a few surprises for the Begotten.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">One of such phenomena is the so called Nightmare Maelstrom. Nightmare Maelstroms are the Primordial Dream's equivalent of a natural disaster. Nobody is really sure about the causes behind them, but Maelstroms happen cyclically and if not properly contained they can cause terrible damages. Maelstroms are thankfully rare, there's no more than one or two for each generation and they happen everywhere in the world, but the tales of those who went through them across the ages circulated and became a recurrent, if somewhat obscure, cautionary tale within Beast's culture.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">During a Maelstrom, an unlucky person becomes the fulcrum of all the dreams and nightmares of a given area. It begins slowly, but a Maelstrom steadily draws towards himself all the oniric streams of a region and grows in power and strenght with time. It breaches the walls that separate the minds of the dreamers, human and supernaturals alike, and brings them together in a unique chaotic nightmare, each night stronger. Eventually, a Maelstrom's presence exerts so much pressure on the texture of reality that the Primordial Dream erupts violently into our world, leaving only destruction behind. All those trapped within it abruptly die of fear, screaming and crying, their collective deathcry resonating for years in the astral.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Only Beasts can hope to survive their aftermath. Their connection to the Primordial Dream and profound understanding of fear protects them from this certain death, but are not immune from the other consequences and are often let traumatized and damaged by the experience. A Beast's Lair is not safe from the Maelstrom and, even if they survive, going through it is often excruciating. The reason why stories of Maelstroms work so well as a scare tactic is that, for what concerns Beast, those disaster happen when a Devouring goes wrong.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">For reasons unknown, a would-be Maelstrom can remain quiescent for all its life. Since their birth they show traces of a bond with the Primordial Dream like Beast and Heroes do, but their oniric identity is always shifting. They suffer from nightmares, but the Horror that stalks them is never the same. Sometimes they fight monsters, something they're the monster itself. Sometimes they dream someone else's dream. It all pretty vivid, but most potential Maelstroms go through all their life without questioning the matter. The problem happens when a Beast proceeds to put one of them through a Devouring. Maelstroms have something that resembles a Horror within themselves, but it's a fake, ever-changing construct that's more a shade of a Horror than a true one. Beasts don't know that. Most importantly, Beast </span></span><i>cannot</i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> know that. For all they know, they're in front of a potential Begotten. If they proceed with the Devouring, the Maelstrom awakens.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">There's no Final Nightmare for a Maelstrom. No epiphany, no neat powers, no Hunger. They're not Beasts and they never were. But after the fake Devouring, things do get weird. Suddenly, they're able to spot monsters and monsters are able to spot them on sight (and are inexplicably drawn to them). Each night they go trough an extremely vivid crucible were they wander around the astral dreamscape and enter the dreams of the sleepers.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Beasts are tricked by the fact that the Maelstrom appears like Family. To be more precise, it seems one of the Begotten, Horror, Lair and all. It's easy to see while many Beasts don't notice its true nature until things take a turn for the worse. For those who know where to look, though, there are signs. First of all, the Maelstrom's \u201cHorror\u201d changes. Each night it is a different one with a different Lair. It's odd, to say the least. The don't have Atavism or Nightmares, nor all the supernatural abilities of a Beast. It's just a facade that only Beasts can notice. In fact, at first Heroes can't even track a Maelstrom. They sense its disturbance over the Primordial Dream, but this only leads them to look after real Beasts. The most glaring difference though, is that Maelstroms are not aware of their condition. They know that something bad it's going on, but they have no control over it: they're victims as well.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">As time goes on, the mere presence of Maelstroms alters the dreams of others, changing the narrative and the events. They'll eventually become able to interact directly with those dreams, with even stronger consequences. When the other dreamers begin to be forced into the Maelstrom's own dream, the event is reaching its final stages. On the last day, every single person in the area aside from Beasts and Heroes cannot wake up and are forced to take part to the oniric apocalypse that's about to happen. The barriers between their dreams crumble as they all become part of the Maelstrom. The Primordial Dream floods all their minds and the barrier that keeps it separate from the real world weakens. The Horrors and their Lairs feast on the screaming crowd and gain enough power to enter the material plane. At the culmination of this, the Maelstrom's soul detonates and brings all the dreamers with it. Some say the Dark Mother herself appears to take the Maelstrom's soul. The Maelstrom itself survives, soulless, traumatized and forever cut away from the Primordial Dream, but alive. Beasts are left to pick up the pieces.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">What can Beast do when a Maelstrom happens? Once they've identified it, there's only a solution: they have to kill it. Not in their dreams, a Maelstrom's astral presence is so strong that it reforms each day if slained or devoured: they have to put an end to its life. Pure and simple. This, obviously, can be a complex feat for a number of reason, the moral one first and foremost. But when left with the choice between saving one life or saving thousands, the dilemma acquires weight. If you consider that more often than not Beast have socialized with a Maelstrom while mistaking it for one of them, it all becomes even more complicated.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Killing someone you don't know is already hard. If that person is a friend, a brother or a lover, the choice becomes even less obvious.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Mechanics:</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Since the Devouring, the Maelstrom goes trough six different phases as it gains power. Each phases lasts for five days, except for the final one which lasts one. This means every Maelstrom lasts for exactly twenty-six days. During those days, the Maelstrom's influence on dreams resonates thematically with a combination of Beast's Families and Hungers, every day a new one. Its fake Horror changes accordingly. One day it might be a Namtaru Tyrant, the following one a Makara Collector and so on. Everyday a different Horror, a different Lair, a different Hunger. There's no precise scheme for this evolution, some spend a entire phase with a given Family or Hunger, some do not. All sleepers in the area are affected by the current shape of the Maelstrom's \u201cHorror\u201d. It speaks great volume that Maelstroms have to inflict all the possible facets of the Beast's condition over the population as their power grows. The last day, though, there's no new Horror: it belongs to the Dark Mother.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The specific rules for each phase are the following:</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Phase 1 (Days 1 \u2013 5)</b><br /> <b>- </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">It counts as having Lair 1 when a roll is required</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- The Maelstrom becomes the Apex. It cannot loose this position until the end.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- The Maelstrom gains Thicker Than Water and Family Resemblance</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- The Maelstrom gains a fake Horror and Lair as specified above. It cannot enter this Lair and has no immunities, though other Beasts can.</span></span><br /> <b>- </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">The Maelstrom becomes immune to the Soul Shocked Condition and its soul cannot be removed in any way.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-At this stage, the Maelstrom merely wanders around dreams. Almost no influence from the fake Horror</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to open a Primordial Pathway get a +1 bonus</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Phase 2 (Days 6 \u2013 10)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- It counts as having Lair 3 when a roll is required</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- At this stage, dreamers begin to notice the Maelstrom. Dreams change accordingly to the current nature of the fake Horror</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to open a Primordial Pathway get a +2 bonus</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Phase 3 (Days 11-15)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- It counts as having Lair 5 when a roll is required</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-At this stage, the current nature of the fake Horror alters the dreams completely. The Maelstrom is able to visit more dreams at once.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to open a Primordial Pathway get a +3 bonus</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Phase 4 (Days 16-20)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- It counts as having Lair 7 when a roll is required</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-At this stage, each dreamer enters the dream of Maelstrom instead and they are swept away from the fake Horror's current nature, but each dream is still separate from the others. People no longer regain Willpower from sleep</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to open a Primordial Pathway get a +4 bonus</span></span><br /> <b>- </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rolls to use Nightmares get a + 1 Bonus</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Phase 5 (Days 21-25)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- It counts as having Lair 9 when a roll is required</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Heroes can track and stalk the Maelstrom like a Beast. Whatever they do with it or if they notice they are not in front of a Beast, it's up to them</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-At this stage, there's no such thing as a single dream. Everyone shares a immense, fragmented nightmare with the Maelstrom at its core. Many gain a Condition such as Delusional, Fatigue, Obsession, Paranoid or Soul-Shocked</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to open a Primordial Pathway get a +5 bonus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to use Nightmares get a + 2 Bonus</span></span><br /> <b>- </b><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Rolls to use Atavisms get a + 1 Bonus</span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Phase 6 (Day 26)</b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- It counts as having Lair 10 when a roll is required.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Every sentient being in the area, except Beast and Heroes, fall asleep and cannot wake up. Supernaturals can roll Resolve + Composure + Supernatural Trait VS the Maelstrom's Resolve + Presence + Lair to resist this effect, but they have to roll each hour unless they leave the area.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Primordial Pathways open around Beasts whether they like it or not, their mere presence enough to alter their surroundings.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to use Nightmares get a + 3 Bonus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- Rolls to use Atavisms get a + 3 Bonus</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- If a Beast sleeps during the last day, her Horror materializes in the real world. It returns to the Lair as soon as the Beast wakes up, but its free to act as it wants in the meantime</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- At the end of the 24 hours everyone caught in the Maelstrom, except Beasts, Heroes and the Maelstrom itself, dies. Mummies are forced into Duat as if slain and Demons' current Covers are shattered and </span></span><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">reduced to 0.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">- If a Maelstrom survives the day, it turns back to normal and gains the Fatigued, Fugue and Soulless Condition</span></span><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"font-size:12px\">Maelstrom have no Satiety, Legend or Life. They cannot have any major supernatural template. They are, tragically, normal human beings whose life is forever changed from the Primordial Dream.</span></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-12-2016, 03:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T06:22:33-08:00","id":829687,"title":"","content":"Does the Maelstrom also reach into other worlds or can changelings and werewolves escape it by entering the hedge or the shadow respectively? Also can mages fight it in the primordial dream which is a portion of the astral?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10574-matthiasthalmann","name":"MatthiasThalmann","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T06:43:58-08:00","id":829692,"title":"","content":"The short answer is no. It does not reach into other worlds. It's something that affects the material and the Primordial Dream and going into those places counts as &quot;leave the area&quot;, even if after a month within the Maelstrom there are probably some minor reflections of its effects in the Shadow.<br /> <br /> Mages, provided they travel deep enough in the Temenos to reach the Primordial Dream, can fight it but it's not of great use. The best they can do is to delay its growth (let's say, if you slain the fake Horror that day does not count for the total of the twenty-six days and the Maelstrom has to go through that specific combination of Horror and Hunger one more time) but its astral form it's too strong and reforms the following day. It usually is not worth the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T07:17:49-08:00","id":829707,"title":"","content":"Damn. I am really liking the Maelstroms, and all the possible story hooks one can cause.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-14T11:19:42-08:00","id":829800,"title":"","content":"Thanks! They're the sort of thing that steals a lot space from other elements in a chronicle and takes a central place, which that makes them not much versatile. Glad to hear you see some potential in them.<br /> <br /> I'm probably returning to low-key, easily exploitable creatures for my next entry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":38,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","user":"Cinder","date":". 02-14-2016, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T08:36:10-08:00","id":1038920,"title":"","content":"I can re-enact one of the best stories from the Sandman comics? Awesome!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:13:32-08:00","id":1038964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1038920#post1038920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can re-enact one of the best stories from the Sandman comics? Awesome!</div> </div> </div> </div>That was the plan. Nice to see you got the reference. I was not subtle at all about it, but when you need to find ideas about creatures and things to populate the Dream you might as well steal from the best.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T10:20:57-08:00","id":1038969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1038964#post1038964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was the plan. Nice to see you got the reference. I was not subtle at all about it, but when you need to find ideas about creatures and things to populate the Dream you might as well steal from the best.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey, nothing wrong with ripping ideas. Saves me the trouble of trying to figure out mechanics for it.<br /> <br /> Will there be any mechanics on how to replicate the way the situation was solved eventually in the comic? Is it even possible?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-27T11:20:14-08:00","id":1038996,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Master Aquatosic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1038969#post1038969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Hey, nothing wrong with ripping ideas. Saves me the trouble of trying to figure out mechanics for it.<br /> <br /> Will there be any mechanics on how to replicate the way the situation was solved eventually in the comic? Is it even possible?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd personally say that belongs to the realm of Storyteller's hands. In short, for the comics it was Rose's grandmother that took her place, but someone still had to die. Even Dream could not find another solution.<br /> <br /> You can plan it out in order to give the players the option, if they really want to and find a person (probably a related one) willing to take the Maelstrom's place, sure.<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you can exploit the Beast part of the arc and go for a solution that lies in the depths of the Primordial Dream and/or involves the Dark Mother. This might be more feasible once we learn more about it with the Player's Guide, but still.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T03:13:08-08:00","id":1043904,"title":"","content":"Hmm. Here's an idea. Seeing as the Primordial Dream is the collective personification of fears, is it possible that there are some native entities/goetia who embody the fear of (natural) disasters and calamities? If so, I imagine their Numina could take the form of Lair Traits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T07:27:28-08:00","id":1043977,"title":"","content":"I think that's what Ravagers are<br /> <br /> EDIT: Insatiables too in a weird way","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 04-24-2017, 01:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-24T15:47:00-07:00","id":1083209,"title":"","content":"I have noticed that my (bare bones) beast tamer rules (in my signature) aren't in this thread. I have been too busy to work on them lately, so maybe some nice homebrewer can adopt them for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T03:48:39-07:00","id":1083397,"title":"","content":"I'd like to add something here.. or atleast place the idea out there for people.... An addition to the Heroes journey in Beast (Esspecially since it doesn't seem to have been touched upon in the Corebook) Heros Regnans or Heros Ascendant.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Regnans</b></u><br /> <br /> <i>&quot;Heros will always be remembered,<br /> But you know legends never Die&quot;<br /> Emperors New Clothes, Panic at the Disco.</i><br /> <br /> Heroes are trouble. They are dangerous, they hunt and kill for their own amusement and hungers, yet they cannot look past what they have become. For all they wish to be the center or the story they are just asmuch a pawn in the narrative. They cannot look past their own gain or needs, this is there role and wants. But what happens when a Hero becomes an Apex?<br /> <br /> Sometimes a Hero becomes so feared and strong in a hive that they simply cannot be stopped, they begin hunting and slaying the Begotten in there own lairs, making themselves have the largest impact upon the Dream in the local area, they become Monsters of their own making, slaugtering the Children and shaping themselves into a Horror of Horrors. They Change, they lose all pretext of humanity and become something else.<br /> <br /> Heros Regnans or Heros Ascendant without the flowery words are Monsterous Heroes that have became what they hunt but are still so wrapped up in their own Tale that they do not understand they are asbad or in many cases Worse then what they hunt. They are the Terrifying Vigilante whose mear mention makes people blanch and hide, they are mob boss who doesn't just kill you for your betrayal, no they make EVERYONE suffer. They kill all your family, friends and associates, leaving you alone, a Pariah amongst society, only then will they finish you.<br /> <br /> (Will add more as i write it)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:55:11-07:00","id":1083589,"title":"","content":"Leliel said this, so I take no responsibility or credit. I just thought that it was a kinda cool idea and decided to post it over here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1074499-persona-5-is-beast-the-primordial-from-the-heroes-perspective?p=1082734#post1082734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though, actually...<br /> <br /> I think Palace Keepers are a good antagonist; they're humans who have grown so feared and hated by people around them that they've essentially become the local Apex of their Hive. Not the entire Hive, mind, but they exert enough influence to form an echo of themselves in the Dream, and that forms a free-floating Lair whose purpose is to give its unknowing master whatever they want. This manifests in many ways, but one is invariably as a steadfast refusal of the people around them to censure their behavior for whatever reason; because they're key to the group, they're too strong, they &quot;mean so well&quot;...<br /> <br /> Needless to say, Beast enjoy crushing them, both for the free Chambers and you don't become the Apex without any supernatural touch at all by being a nice person.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T11:57:23-07:00","id":1083594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1083397#post1083397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd like to add something here.. or atleast place the idea out there for people.... An addition to the Heroes journey in Beast (Esspecially since it doesn't seem to have been touched upon in the Corebook) Heros Regnans or Heros Ascendant.<br /> <br /> <u><b>Regnans</b></u></div> </div> </div> </div>Much as I like the idea, I can't help but feel that you might want to alter the name slightly. Perhaps the Hero Resplendent? The Hero Regnant? Regnans doesn't really make all that much sense. Also, it's 'heroes'. Sorry. That's my Horror talking; the infamous Grammar Nazi.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-25T14:00:58-07:00","id":1083672,"title":"","content":"Other topics:<ul><li><b>Dreamtides</b> - less... cataclysmic intrusions (compared to Maelstroms) of the Dream upon the waking World. Similar to when a Beast overlays their Lair upon an area, but larger and not directed by an intelligence.<ul><li>Smaller manifestations could be confused with hauntings, or faerie circles (from when someone wanders in, but doesn't get out before the effect fades).</li> <li>Need a mysterious Dark Scary Forest that only appears on some nights? The Dream intrudes. Better escape before the convergence ends, and you are trapped in the Dream.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Mythic Items</b> - The Primordial Dream made manifest in (or through) an object of repute. Dreaded Weapons, Cursed Artifacts, etc. The Legend of the thing gives it power, and warps the narrative/destiny of those around it.</li> <li><b>[Atavisms?]</b> - Flora and Fauna touched by the Primordial Dream, and perhaps have undergone a lesser Devouring of their own. Mutated, material counterparts to Night Terrors. Not the manifest Fear-of-Bears, but a real bear touched/invested by Fear.<ul><li>[Might be redundant with Night Terror!Claimed]</li> <li>[If not redundant, maybe stick an Atavism or few on a creature/plant, give it a Legend, optional Anathema, call it good? Getting chased by a bear with Relentless Hunter or a rat with Looming Presence is pretty scary. Even a tree with Stormwracked(?) has some potential.]</li> </ul></li> <li><b>Formidolosii</b> - People afflicted by a connection to the Primordial Dream. They become vectors for Nightmares, spreading them either deliberately or unwillingly (when suffering their own Breaking Points, or when a Condition triggers from letting the fear build up). Not Heroes, not Beasts, but something else. Maybe they are a &quot;release valve&quot; for pent up fears stuck in the Dream. Might make a decent Minor Template.</li> <li><b>Odd Kinships</b> - Strange locations that Beasts can form Kinships to. Maybe the ability to form Kinships with the <b>Mythic Items</b> above for extra perks. Maybe adding a Z-splat (tentative name <b>Colleges</b>, as a nod to the &quot;teaching culture&quot;) for Beasts to form Kinship (and Kinship Nightmares) to philosophies and modes of thought.</li> <li><b>Catharsi</b> - Lesser beings, similar to Night Terrors (but probably from the Bright Dream) that represent the emotional and stress relief that Fear can provide. Probably few in number, unfortunately.</li> </ul>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 04-25-2017, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T00:25:05-07:00","id":1083880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1083594#post1083594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Much as I like the idea, I can't help but feel that you might want to alter the name slightly. Perhaps the Hero Resplendent? The Hero Regnant? Regnans doesn't really make all that much sense. Also, it's 'heroes'. Sorry. That's my Horror talking; the infamous Grammar Nazi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well Regnan was a literal translation of Ascendant into Latin (according to google translate, yeah not the greatest source) the name can be changed into something abit better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Light and Dark are two Sides of a Coin... Humanity is What Happens when it Lands on it's Edge.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3981-rickmanuk","name":"RickmanUK","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3981_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"533"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-26T00:44:30-07:00","id":1083882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RickmanUK</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/821719-nightmares-dreamscapes-incursions-from-the-primordial-dream?p=1083880#post1083880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well Regnan was a literal translation of Ascendant into Latin (according to google translate, yeah not the greatest source) the name can be changed into something abit better.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. You know, you could probably just use 'Ascendant'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":